import csv,json,re
from pathlib import Path
b=Path(__file__).resolve().parent;q=list(csv.DictReader((b/'queue.csv').open()));gg=json.loads((b/'lead-gaia-covariance.json').read_text());cl=json.loads((b/'lead-clocks.json').read_text());iv={r['tic']:r for r in json.loads((b/'lead-current-sector-inventory.json').read_text())}
notes={
'16807424':('PLAUSIBLE','UNESTABLISHED_SINGLE','A sparse localized S21 low cluster near1896.88BTJD has baseline on both sides. A trapezoid gives roughly2.8ppt depth. S48 is noisier and does not demonstrate a repeat.','Only one credible low cluster. Its nearest source-specific Gaia conjunction is about17.16d away versus local covariance sigma1.64d; Gaia association is disfavored. A single event cannot establish a free eclipse clock.','Obtain source-resolved recurrence and a new eclipse timing.'),
'21623270':('PLAUSIBLE','UNESTABLISHED_SINGLE','The S22 cluster near1917.52BTJD is a possible narrow shallow event, approximately2.2ppt in a local trapezoid. Broad S49 settling/trough structure and noisy S76 do not establish a same-kind repeat.','The low cluster is sparsely sampled. The nearest Gaia conjunction differs by7.15d versus local covariance sigma0.84d. No measured recurrence or target ownership is established.','Repeat at a measured free period and resolve the spatial source.'),
'25073050':('C','GAIA_CONSISTENT_TARGET_ATTRIBUTED','S80 contains two matching shallow eclipses centered3480.81500 and3505.10663BTJD, depth about62ppt and duration0.704d. A deep approximately172ppt eclipse at3493.14654BTJD is the other conjunction, not a third same-kind repeat. The measured same-kind interval24.291620859d is close to Gaia24.285909256d. Independent custom aperture reproduces the eclipse and the deficit is target-centered.','The clock has only one same-kind interval. The capable G12.52 neighbor25.07arcsec away is spatially distinguished: all three background-corrected deficit centroids stay0.085-0.234pixel from the target versus1.25-1.36pixels from that neighbor under varied windows. This empirical localization has no calibrated PRF astrometric uncertainty; bandpass and throughput are approximate. No precision long-baseline ephemeris is claimed. The deep event has a data gap truncating egress.','Obtain another same-kind eclipse and source-resolved follow-up.'),
'25796372':('PLAUSIBLE','UNESTABLISHED_SINGLE','S17 shows a broad shallow low interval around1768.3BTJD, approximately1–2ppt, with recovery over days. It may be a single broad eclipse or smooth variability. The bounded trapezoid fit is unusable and no measured center or duration is adopted.','Only one sector exists in the successful current availability check. Low contrast and smooth morphology prevent an eclipse or periodicity claim. The untrusted fit proxy is not a timing or independent geometry measurement.','Obtain a sharp resolved ingress/egress or an independently measured repeat.'),
'41553596':('PLAUSIBLE','UNESTABLISHED_MULTIPLE_SHAPES','S12 has a broad approximately5–6ppt depression near1626.3BTJD and another lower trough near1640.8. S38 has a much narrower low feature near2334.36. Their substantially different widths and sector-edge context do not establish same-kind recurrence. Later sectors contain noise, steps, settling and gaps.','No eclipse clock was fitted from these unlike features. Treating1626.3 and2334.36 as29 cycles merely assumes an untested alias. The nearby VSX SR|M source24.54arcsec away is a variable contaminant, not an exact eclipsing identification.','Measure recurrence with consistent morphology and spatially separate the nearby variable.'),
'47853068':('PLAUSIBLE','UNESTABLISHED_SINGLE','The noisy variable S87 baseline contains a possible bounded depression around3677.8BTJD, approximately8ppt in a local fit, amid post-gap settling and elevated scatter. S6 andS33 do not demonstrate recurrence.','No same-kind eclipse clock. Gaia-conjunction mismatch is about13.52d with local covariance sigma3.59d. NewS107–109 availability is explicitly investigated by the helper; a missing or noise-limited window is not a clean null.','Obtain cleaner source-resolved event morphology and recurrence.'),
'86515505':('PLAUSIBLE','UNESTABLISHED_PARTIAL_SINGLE','The S13 low cluster descends into the data gap: last good cadence1667.68291BTJD. The cluster is visible in raw flux but recovery is missing. The trial trapezoid extrapolates its center beyond observed data and is explicitly unusable. S39 has a low post-gap settling edge, whileS66,S93,S104 show broad variability or settling rather than a demonstrated same-kind repeat.','The queue visual description of bounded recovery is not supported by the deciding raw mask. No measured eclipse center, period or duration is adopted. The geometry entry for this trial is only an unusable fit proxy.','Observe a complete bounded event with source attribution and repeat timing.'),
'130609636':('PLAUSIBLE','UNESTABLISHED_PARTIAL_SINGLE','S91 shows a deep localized V-shaped partial event near3789.52BTJD with roughly34–38ppt loss and a clear recovery. Ingress is partly lost in a0.19d gap. S46 contains only much shallower noisy excursions, not a matching repeat.','One partial event, no free recurrence period. The symmetric local fit is retained as an approximate shape proxy but excluded from usable precision timings. Gaia geometry is broadly compatible within uncertainty and is not an independent validation of a single event.','Obtain another same-kind event and resolve the eclipsing source.')}
rows=[]
for r in q:
 t=r['tic'];v,a,reason,lim,nxt=notes[t];g=gg[t];ev=json.loads((b/t/'lead-timing.json').read_text());c=cl.get(t);p=b/t/'REPORT.md';inv=iv[t]
 lines=[f"# {r['sample_id']}: TIC {t}",f"Full review completion: COMPLETE_BOUNDED. Physical verdict: {v}. Association: {a}.",reason,'## Exact selection and provenance',f"Exact frozen queue row, Gaia DR3 {r['gaia_dr3']}, nested Gaia G={r['gaia_G']}. No substitution. Parent fresh-band-next1000; operational group first/batch03 is provenance, not a scientific rank. The single_discrete visual stratum is selected follow-up, not a blind yield denominator. Queue visual_reason is historical triage and can be contradicted by raw review.",'Identity-audit.json verifies exact Gaia/TIC identity, nested magnitudes, FITS TIC/sector headers, and every parent QLP SHA256. Bulk-results and appointment-results retain per-window scores, trial durations, coverage, masks and nonflags for near-threshold revisiting. No additional threshold was imposed here. Lead-context flag_events includes every saved dip window, including nonflags, despite its historical name.','## Raw flux and timing','Finite TIME, finite positive SAP_FLUX and QUALITY=0. Raw full-sector and local plots were personally inspected by the lead. KSPSAP where present is an alternate reduction of the same photons. Same-kind versus opposite conjunction was judged before fitting. Local linear-baseline trapezoid errors are conditional formal errors, not calibrated astrophysical accuracy. Boundary, partial and extrapolated fits are unusable for precision timing.','| Sector | Kind | Trial center BTJD | Trial depth ppt | Timing usable |','|---|---|---:|---:|---|']
 for e in ev:lines.append(f"| {e['sector']} | {e['kind']} | {e.get('center_btjd',0):.6f} | {e.get('depth_ppt',0):.2f} | {e.get('fit_usable',False)} |")
 if c:
  aa=json.loads((b/'lead-alias-covered-windows.json').read_text())[t]
  lines+=['## Clock and aliases',f"Same-kind period={c['period_d']:.9f}d from cycles0,1; epoch3480.815004BTJD is the shallow-kind epoch, not the deeper primary. Formal difference error={c['formal_period_error_d']:.8f}d after0.002d/event floor. A heuristic0.02d allowance describes baseline/shape limitations and is not calibrated coverage. No O-C scatter follows from two points. Deep event phase={c['deep_phase']:.6f}. TESS sector80 common absolute timing offset largely cancels in this same-sector interval.",'Divisors3–6 predict covered clean nulls and are rejected. The half-period combines alternating depths and the deep event is displaced from the shallow half-clock by0.186d, so it is not a same-kind period. Doubling fails to map both observed shallow events to one conjunction; a two-orbit interpretation is not established. The bounded tested alternatives, masks and per-window values are in lead-alias-covered-windows.json. Core coverage>=75%, no large core gap and both sidebands are required. Null condition depth+4*local point scatter < half characteristic depth is deliberately conservative; missing/flagged windows are not nulls.','| Trial | Period d | Timing compatible | Covered | Clean nulls |','|---|---:|---|---:|---:|']
  for z in aa:lines.append(f"| {z['label']} | {z['period_d']:.8f} | {z['timing_compatible']} | {z['covered']} | {len(z['nulls'])} |")
 else:lines+=['## Recurrence and availability','No same-kind period is measured. Sparse or unlike events are not assigned integer cycle counts. The saved conditional Gaia-period coverage is an audit aid only; it does not establish the period or prove every unobserved prediction absent. Missing data and noise-limited windows remain explicit.']
 lines +=[f"Current TESScut sector inventory checked{inv['checked_utc']}: {inv.get('tesscut_sectors',[])}. Original QLP inventory: {inv['qlp_all_sectors']}. Response/status/hashes in lead-current-sector-inventory.json. Availability is not proof of usable eclipse coverage.",'## Independent reduction and source attribution','HELPER-AUDIT.md and target helper artifacts document custom TESScut apertures, difference images and Gaia neighbors where informative, including unavailable or inconclusive checks. These reductions share the same TESS photons; separate sectors are separate occasions. A centered deficit must be distinguished from capable neighbors before confirmation; a capable unresolved blend retains host uncertainty. Unperformed work is not silently a successful check.','## Gaia geometry',f"Source-specific P={g['gaia_period_d']:.9f} +/- {g['gaia_period_error_d']:.8g}d, e={g['eccentricity']:.6f}, omega={g['omega_deg']:.5f}deg, Tp={g['tp_btjd']:.6f}BTJD, mass function={g['mass_function_solar']:.6g}solar masses. The lead-gaia-covariance artifact uses each source's P,e,omega,Tp correlation submatrix with fixed-cycle local linear propagation and edge-on conjunctions. Unusable fits remain labeled; their proxy offsets are not independent timing evidence. Broad covariance consistency is not source-ownership proof or a full nonlinear orbit posterior.",'## Catalogue status','Physical classification and novelty remain separate. Root-owned shared-catalogues/ROOT-CATALOGUE-SEAL.json covers successful VSX/ASAS-SN cones, SIMBAD exact IDs, Gaia EB and variability tables, Prsa/IJspeert/Kostov comparisons, Kepler/K2 and TOI checks and bounded identity/literature searches. No exact prior EB identification appears for these eight in that scope. The Z021 nearby SR|M entry is retained separately. Failed or absent queries are unknown; a scoped nonmatch does not prove exhaustive priority. No plausible row is a counted new system.','## Limitations and next check',lim,nxt,'## Evidence',f"Target lead-context.json, lead-series.json, lead-timing.json, lead-fullsectors.png, lead-raw-context.png, selected-event plot and helper artifacts; batch lead-clocks.json, lead-alias-covered-windows.json, lead-single-conditional-coverage.json, identity-audit.json, lead-gaia-covariance.json, HELPER-AUDIT.md, LEAD-AUDIT.md and SOURCE-MANIFEST.json."]
 p.write_text('\n\n'.join(lines)+'\n',encoding='utf8');rows.append(dict(sample_id=r['sample_id'],tic=t,gaia_dr3=r['gaia_dr3'],physical_verdict=v,full_review_completion='COMPLETE_BOUNDED',period_days=f"{c['period_d']:.9f}" if c else '',period_interpretation='single same-kind interval; shallow-kind epoch' if c else 'not measured',association=a,limitations=lim,next_check=nxt,report=str(p)))
with (b/'RESULTS.csv').open('w',newline='',encoding='utf8') as f:w=csv.DictWriter(f,fieldnames=rows[0]);w.writeheader();w.writerows(rows)
